{
  "id": "m05-range-add-final",
  "title": "Paint Strips",
  "source": {
    "name": "Classic range-update exercise; compare CSES 'Range Update Queries' (offline version)",
    "url": "https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1651"
  },
  "rating": 1100,
  "tags": [
    "difference-array",
    "arrays"
  ],
  "statement": "You have an array of `n` integers. You then apply `q` updates in order; update `l r x` adds `x` to every element from position `l` to position `r` (1-indexed, inclusive). After all updates, print the final array.\n\n**Input.** First line `n q`. Second line the `n` initial values. Then `q` lines, each `l r x`.\n\n**Output.** One line with the `n` final values separated by spaces.\n\n**Example.**\n\nInput:\n```\n5 3\n0 0 0 0 0\n1 3 2\n2 5 3\n4 4 -1\n```\nOutput:\n```\n2 5 5 2 3\n```",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n, q ≤ 800 in this browser version (the idea scales to 2·10^5)",
    "−10^9 ≤ initial values ≤ 10^9",
    "−10^6 ≤ x ≤ 10^6",
    "1 ≤ l ≤ r ≤ n"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 1000,
  "tests": [
    {
      "input": "5 3\n0 0 0 0 0\n1 3 2\n2 5 3\n4 4 -1\n",
      "output": "2 5 5 2 3\n",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
