  "editorial": "Keep a difference array `d` where the value added at position `i` equals the running sum `d[0] + ... + d[i]`. An update `(l, r, x)` becomes `d[l-1] += x` (the increase starts here) and `d[r] -= x` (it stops after position `r`). Each update is `O(1)`. At the end one prefix-sum pass produces the total added at each position.\n\nWithout the trick the cost is `O(nq)`. Remember `d` needs `n + 1` slots so that `r = n` does not write out of range.",
